<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhiwallon ap Cynfyn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1070</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rhiwallon ap Cynfyn was a Welsh king who, with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bleddyn-ap-cynfyn">Bleddyn ap Cynfyn</a>, was set up as ruler of Gwynedd and Powys under the overlordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gruffydd-ap-llywelyn">Gruffudd ap Llywelyn</a> in 1063. The brothers joined English rebels against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a> in 1068. Rhiwallon was killed at the Battle of Mechain in 1070.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhiwallon-ap-cynfyn.jpg" alt="Rhiwallon ap Cynfyn" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Powell and Humphrey Lloyd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AeddanapBlegywryd_or_RhiwallonapCynfyn_historieofcambria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
